---
description: Rules for organizing code in app/libs and app/services directories
globs: app/libs/**/*.js,app/services/**/*.js
alwaysApply: false
---

# Libs vs services (minimal)

## `app/libs`

- Infrastructure and integrations (auth setup, db clients, queue, third-party SDK wrappers).
- Keep modules reusable and low-level.
- Do not put domain workflows here.

## `app/services`

- Domain/business workflows that orchestrate libs and persistence.
- Services may depend on libs and other services.

## Dependency boundary

- `services -> libs` is allowed.
- `libs -> services` is not allowed.

## File pattern

- Prefer `*.server.js` for server-only modules in both directories.
- Use `#/*` imports and omit extensions.
